  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "The development permitted shall be begun before the expiration of five years from the date of this permission.  REASON:\tIn order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990. | All external materials to be used in the development shall match the appearance of those of the existing building.   REASON:\tTo ensure that the materials harmonise with the surroundings, in accordance with policies 4.1, 5.5 and 5.9 of the adopted Ealing Unitary Development Plan, 'Plan for the Environment' (2004). | Before any works commence on site, details of a scheme to provide parking for cyclists in accordance with adopted standards shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, and such details as approved shall be implemented and brought into use prior to first occupation, and retained permanently.  REASON:\tTo provide adequate facilities for cyclists, in accordance with policy 9.6 of the adopted Ealing Unitary Development Plan, 'Plan for the Environment' (2004). | No part of the roof of the extension shall be used as or altered to form a balcony, roof garden, roof terrace or similar amenity area.  REASON:  To protect the living conditions of occupants of nearby properties, in accordance with policies 4.1, 5.5 and 5.9 of the adopted Ealing Unitary Development Plan, 'Plan for the Environment' (2004). | Details of dustbin and enclosed refuse areas shall be submitted to and approved by the Local Planning Authority, and the details as approved shall be implemented on the bring into use of the development, and shall thereafter be retained.   REASON:\tTo ensure that adequate refuse facilities are provided on the site, in accordance with policy 5.5 of the adopted Ealing Unitary Development Plan, 'Plan for the Environment' (2004)."
  ],
